msgstr "Nocturne is a modern, open-source rewrite of the Nightscout diabetes management platform. Built on .NET 10 with a SvelteKit frontend, it provides the same API compatibility as Nightscout while offering improved performance, modern architecture, and easier deployment."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "How does Nocturne compare to Nightscout?"
msgstr "How does Nocturne compare to Nightscout?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Nocturne is API-compatible with Nightscout (v1, v2, and v3 APIs), so your existing apps and devices work without changes. The main differences are under the hood: Nocturne uses PostgreSQL instead of MongoDB, is built on .NET for better performance, and includes modern tooling like Aspire for orchestration and observability."
msgstr "Nocturne is API-compatible with Nightscout (v1, v2, and v3 APIs), so your existing apps and devices work without changes. The main differences are under the hood: Nocturne uses PostgreSQL instead of MongoDB, is built on .NET for better performance, and includes modern tooling like Aspire for orchestration and observability."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Is Nocturne free?"
msgstr "Is Nocturne free?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Who is Nocturne for?"
msgstr "Who is Nocturne for?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Nocturne is for anyone who uses Nightscout or wants to self-host their diabetes data. Whether you're using a DIY closed loop system, want to share your glucose data with caregivers, or just want to track your data independently, Nocturne can help."
msgstr "Nocturne is for anyone who uses Nightscout or wants to self-host their diabetes data. Whether you're using a DIY closed loop system, want to share your glucose data with caregivers, or just want to track your data independently, Nocturne can help."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "What are the system requirements?"
msgstr "What are the system requirements?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Nocturne requires Docker to run. Any system that can run Docker (Linux, Windows, macOS) can host Nocturne. For a single user, a small VPS with 1GB RAM is sufficient. For families or multiple users, we recommend 2GB+ RAM."
msgstr "Nocturne requires Docker to run. Any system that can run Docker (Linux, Windows, macOS) can host Nocturne. For a single user, a small VPS with 1GB RAM is sufficient. For families or multiple users, we recommend 2GB+ RAM."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Can I run Nocturne on a Raspberry Pi?"
msgstr "Can I run Nocturne on a Raspberry Pi?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Yes! Nocturne runs well on Raspberry Pi 4 and newer models. The ARM64 Docker images are available for these platforms."
msgstr "Yes! Nocturne runs well on Raspberry Pi 4 and newer models. The ARM64 Docker images are available for these platforms."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Do I need technical knowledge to set up Nocturne?"
msgstr "Do I need technical knowledge to set up Nocturne?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Basic familiarity with Docker and command line is helpful, but our configuration wizard generates all the files you need. Most users can get up and running by following our getting started guide."
msgstr "Basic familiarity with Docker and command line is helpful, but our configuration wizard generates all the files you need. Most users can get up and running by following our getting started guide."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Can I use an existing PostgreSQL database?"
msgstr "Can I use an existing PostgreSQL database?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Yes! While Nocturne includes a PostgreSQL container by default, you can configure it to use any external PostgreSQL database. This is useful if you already have managed database hosting."
msgstr "Yes! While Nocturne includes a PostgreSQL container by default, you can configure it to use any external PostgreSQL database. This is useful if you already have managed database hosting."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Migration"
msgstr "Migration"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Can I migrate my existing Nightscout data?"
msgstr "Can I migrate my existing Nightscout data?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Yes! Nocturne includes built-in migration tools to import your complete history from Nightscout. Your entries, treatments, and profile data can all be imported."
msgstr "Yes! Nocturne includes built-in migration tools to import your complete history from Nightscout. Your entries, treatments, and profile data can all be imported."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Will my existing apps still work?"
msgstr "Will my existing apps still work?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Yes! Nocturne is fully API-compatible with Nightscout. xDrip+, Loop, AndroidAPS, and other apps that work with Nightscout will work with Nocturne without any configuration changes (just point them to your new Nocturne URL)."
msgstr "Yes! Nocturne is fully API-compatible with Nightscout. xDrip+, Loop, AndroidAPS, and other apps that work with Nightscout will work with Nocturne without any configuration changes (just point them to your new Nocturne URL)."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Can I run Nocturne alongside Nightscout?"
msgstr "Can I run Nocturne alongside Nightscout?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Yes! The Compatibility Proxy mode lets you run Nocturne alongside your existing Nightscout instance. This is great for testing Nocturne before fully migrating."
msgstr "Yes! The Compatibility Proxy mode lets you run Nocturne alongside your existing Nightscout instance. This is great for testing Nocturne before fully migrating."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "What happens to my Nightscout during migration?"
msgstr "What happens to my Nightscout during migration?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Migration is read-only - it copies data from Nightscout without modifying your original instance. You can keep your Nightscout running during and after migration until you're confident in your Nocturne setup."
msgstr "Migration is read-only - it copies data from Nightscout without modifying your original instance. You can keep your Nightscout running during and after migration until you're confident in your Nocturne setup."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Technical"
msgstr "Technical"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "What technology stack does Nocturne use?"
msgstr "What technology stack does Nocturne use?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Nocturne is built on .NET 10 for the backend API, PostgreSQL for data storage, and SvelteKit 2 with Svelte 5 for the frontend. It uses .NET Aspire for service orchestration and observability."
msgstr "Nocturne is built on .NET 10 for the backend API, PostgreSQL for data storage, and SvelteKit 2 with Svelte 5 for the frontend. It uses .NET Aspire for service orchestration and observability."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "How do data connectors work?"
msgstr "How do data connectors work?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Connectors are background services that fetch data from external sources like Dexcom Share or LibreView. Each connector authenticates with its data source and periodically syncs glucose readings to your Nocturne instance."
msgstr "Connectors are background services that fetch data from external sources like Dexcom Share or LibreView. Each connector authenticates with its data source and periodically syncs glucose readings to your Nocturne instance."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Is there an API?"
msgstr "Is there an API?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Yes! Nocturne implements the full Nightscout API (v1, v2, and v3) plus additional endpoints. Interactive API documentation is available through Scalar when enabled."
msgstr "Yes! Nocturne implements the full Nightscout API (v1, v2, and v3) plus additional endpoints. Interactive API documentation is available through Scalar when enabled."

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Can I contribute to Nocturne?"
msgstr "Can I contribute to Nocturne?"

#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Absolutely! Nocturne is open source and welcomes contributions. Check out our GitHub repository for contribution guidelines, or join the community to discuss features and improvements."
msgstr "Absolutely! Nocturne is open source and welcomes contributions. Check out our GitHub repository for contribution guidelines, or join the community to discuss features and improvements."

